  AND g.segments = '[{"r":"こ","t":"故"},{"t":" is the kanji assigned to it; the "},{"t":"こ"},{"t":" of "},{"r":"じこ","t":"事故"},{"t":" is that character''s unrelated Chinese reading. It is an ordinary noun, which is why it takes "},{"t":"の"},{"t":" after another noun: "},{"r":"やまいけ","t":"病気"},{"t":"ゆえに"},{"t":", "},{"r":"まず","t":"貧"},{"t":"しさの"},{"r":"こ","t":"故"},{"t":"に"},{"t":".\n\nIt is the most formal of the reason words, above "},{"t":"ため"},{"t":" and "},{"t":"から"},{"t":", because it survives mainly in classical and written registers. Descartes in Japanese is "},{"r":"われ","t":"我"},{"r":"おも","t":"思"},{"t":"う"},{"t":"、"},{"t":"ゆえに"},{"r":"われ","t":"我"},{"t":"あり"},{"t":", and the register is exactly right for it."}]'::jsonb
