("},{"r":"よ","t":"読"},{"t":"みやすかった"},{"t":", "},{"r":"よ","t":"読"},{"t":"みにくくない"},{"t":"), because an adjective is what they still are.\n\n"},{"r":"にく","t":"難"},{"t":"い"},{"t":" is worth following further. It survives in "},{"r":"あ","t":"有"},{"t":"り"},{"r":"にく","t":"難"},{"t":"い"},{"t":", \"difficult to exist\", said of something so rare it is precious; and that word, worn down, is "},{"t":"ありがとう"},{"t":". The word for thank you is an adjective meaning hard to come by."}]}'::jsonb, 'ai', 900, 'pending'
