  AND g.segments = '[{"t":"まじ"},{"t":" negated "},{"t":"べし"},{"t":". Where "},{"t":"べし"},{"t":" said something should or would be, "},{"t":"まじ"},{"t":" said it should not or would not, and "},{"t":"まい"},{"t":" is what survives of it.\n\nIt kept both of "},{"t":"べし"},{"t":"''s senses. "},{"r":"あめ","t":"雨"},{"t":"は"},{"r":"ふ","t":"降"},{"t":"るまい"},{"t":" is conjecture (surely not); "},{"r":"りゃん","t":"二"},{"r":"たび","t":"度"},{"t":"と"},{"r":"い","t":"行"},{"t":"くまい"},{"t":" is resolve (I will not). The two readings textbooks list separately are the one auxiliary. Which you get depends on the subject and on whether the verb names something one can will: "},{"r":"わちき","t":"私"},{"t":"はもう"},{"r":"なが","t":"長"},{"t":"くは"},{"r":"い","t":"生"},{"t":"きられまい"},{"t":" is first person and still pure conjecture."}]'::jsonb
