  AND g.segments = '[{"r":"たい","t":"対"},{"t":" is the "},{"r":"たい","t":"対"},{"t":" of "},{"r":"はんたい","t":"反対"},{"t":" and "},{"r":"たいりつ","t":"対立"},{"t":": one thing set facing another. "},{"t":"に"},{"r":"たい","t":"対"},{"t":"して"},{"t":" puts the sentence in that posture.\n\nBoth senses follow from the picture. Facing someone is directing something at them ("},{"r":"わちき","t":"私"},{"t":"に"},{"r":"たい","t":"対"},{"t":"して"},{"r":"しつれい","t":"失礼"},{"t":"だ"},{"t":"); facing something is being set against it, which gives the contrastive reading ("},{"r":"にい","t":"兄"},{"t":"に"},{"r":"たい","t":"対"},{"t":"して"},{"r":"おとと","t":"弟"},{"t":"は"},{"r":"しず","t":"静"},{"t":"かだ"},{"t":"). Same stance, read forwards or sideways."}]'::jsonb
