  AND g.segments = '[{"r":"かわ","t":"川"},{"t":"に"},{"r":"そ","t":"沿"},{"t":"って"},{"r":"ある","t":"歩"},{"t":"く"},{"t":" is the literal use, and it is still the commonest one. The pattern keeps the picture of two things lying parallel.\n\nWhich is why "},{"t":"に"},{"r":"そ","t":"沿"},{"t":"って"},{"t":" covers both a physical line ("},{"r":"たお","t":"道"},{"t":"に"},{"r":"そ","t":"沿"},{"t":"って"},{"t":") and an abstract one ("},{"r":"ほうしん","t":"方針"},{"t":"に"},{"r":"そ","t":"沿"},{"t":"って"},{"t":"): a policy is something you keep beside rather than something you are fastened to. That is the difference from "},{"t":"に"},{"r":"もと","t":"基"},{"t":"づいて"},{"t":"."}]'::jsonb
